{"term":"oasis","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:590f45d9c351c719df","definition":"A spring of fresh water, surrounded by a fertile region of vegetation, in a desert.","example":"It was the Lost Oasis, the Oasis of the vision in the sand. […] Deep-hidden in the hollow, beneath the cliffs, it lay; and round it the happy verdure spread for many a rood. […] Yes, the quest was ended, the Lost Oasis was the Found!","pos":"noun","synonyms":["island","refuge"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["food oasis","highway oasis","Kharga Oasis","oasification","Oasisamerica","oasisless","oasislike"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oasis#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f03585e187c43dd55","definition":"A quiet, peaceful place or situation separated from surrounding noise or bustle.","example":"The park was an oasis in the middle of the busy city.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["food oasis","highway oasis","Kharga Oasis","oasification","Oasisamerica","oasisless","oasislike"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oasis#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:67bfe3be67ff4539ee","definition":"A place or situation of fruitfulness or abundance separated from surrounding barrenness or scarcity.","example":"[T]here is no true American music but the wild sweet melodies of the Negro slave; the American fairy tales and folklore are Indian and African; and, all in all, we black men seem the sole oasis of simple faith and reverence in a dusty desert of dollars and smartness.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["food oasis","highway oasis","Kharga Oasis","oasificatio